Files and mechanism

scripts/landing.py:1171 records_gate_delta uses git diff --quiet C Cprime -- .
':!.bboxy'. This rejects any non-records tree delta, including renames and mode
changes. The new candidate must verify as signed. git diff --no-renames collects
both sides of records renames; each changed path must have no fixed-string match
in code under crates, scripts, Makefile, verification or lab.

scripts/landing.py:1189 gate_proof still requires exactly one completed full normal
source/result pair, a green completion and an intact formal receipt for the
original tested source. An R5-eligible rebase runs the records gates on the
existing private checking checkout of Cprime. Untracked author-tree records cannot
satisfy those gates. All current model, source-input and tool hashes must still
match the old archive before the records checks run.

scripts/landing.py:627 records_checks runs the records-push gate set: doc corpus
(including links), mermaid, layering, pending-flags, kill-own-pids,
generated-sources, licenses, brand, images, cross-os and never-block. A changed-
record secret scan runs first and reads stored Git blobs, without following a
record symlink outside the repository or printing matching bytes. The normal
conditional e2e check remains in that shared set; an R5 delta naming e2e-acceptance
is refused before these gates because code references it.

scripts/formal.py:276 keeps ordinary receipt validation exact-SHA. The explicit
prior-source validation used by R5 still checks every current inventory, input,
model and tool hash. scripts/formal.py:326 copies the intact checked model
artifacts into a new current-source archive, records the original evidence digest
and records-rebase provenance, and validates the resulting current-source receipt.
Rust tests, model export and TLC do not rerun on this records-only acceptance
path. Repeated remote movement with a supplied log is checked against that log
again, rather than falling through to an unrelated formal refresh.

The landing records the actual full-test source as tested_sha and gate_log_source,
plus records_delta and records_checks_exit=0; formal.source is the new candidate.
Any failed R5 eligibility or records gate refuses gate_log_source_mismatch before
push. CLI help describes the records-only exception.

scripts/test-landing.py:1257-1369 supplies the real Git/private bare-origin process
witnesses. scripts/test-landing-budget-controls.py adds six R5 mutations and a
per-run --out option. verification/README.md, contracts.toml and coverage.toml map
the eligibility/rebinding predicates to implementation tests and the existing
LandingVerification equivalent-input abstraction. No parallel checker or new
claim of arbitrary Rust refinement is introduced.

Acceptance witnesses

(a) An unreferenced decisions record arrives on private origin/main; the old
full-log candidate is rebased and accepted. Exactly the two records Cargo tests
and nine records scripts run; no workspace test, clippy, model export or Java run
is added. An untracked malformed author-tree record cannot affect these checks.
The landing record identifies the old source and precise records delta, and its
new formal receipt passes the default current-source verifier. The old receipt
continues to fail that default verifier on Cprime.
(b) Both a changed Rust source and one tracked byte under crates outside the
formal source inventory are refused. The latter makes the tree guard essential,
so its broken control really publishes to the private bare origin and fails the
named no-accept assertion; it does not merely trip another evidence-hash guard.
(c) Failed corpus/frontmatter checks refuse before push. A code-named
.bboxy/specs/e2e-acceptance.md delta also refuses. Synthetic secret-like content is
refused without echoing its value.
(d) A non-records rename and a pure executable-mode delta are both refused.

