R5 ROUND 2 APPENDIX — task #4915 — 2026-11-01T23:11:35Z

This appendix supersedes earlier current-head and verification-result fields.
Source: a89e6f0cf63c65288af570583e0652bd939df0a2, signed Boxy commit;
parent 6c9d9d7497eef3b6db74f6af53b9471e05a2c2ff. Branch landing-budget,
PR https://github.com/bboxy450/bboxy450-term/pull/89. The new source commit is
pushed; no merge or production land.sh. Only five scoped source/test/verification
files changed (42 insertions, 4 deletions); raw logs remain outside Git.

Executable-record refusal
scripts/landing.py:1193 — records_gate_delta now refuses every changed path
under .bboxy/invariants/ (and replacement of the directory itself), before the
literal name grep and before records checks. The delta inventory uses
--no-renames, so old paths from deletions and renames are also inspected.
scripts/invariants.sh:245 discovers these records with a glob and executes
their check fields. A literal complete-path grep cannot establish equivalence
for such new executable checks. Refusal is gate_log_source_mismatch with the
"executable gate record" detail. Ordinary unreferenced decision records keep
the existing R5 acceptance path and records-only check set.

Submodule hardening
scripts/landing.py:1183 — the outside-record Git tree comparison explicitly
passes --ignore-submodules=none, overriding diff.ignoreSubmodules=all. The
witness changes a real gitlink between committed fixture trees, sets that
local configuration, and requires the typed non-records tree-delta refusal.
It does not depend on a submodule checkout or a network service.

Gate-script glob audit
The retained inventory is target/landing-r5-round2/audit.json, backed by
script-glob-audit.log. Current executable record discovery:
- scripts/invariants.sh:245, .bboxy/invariants/*.md: check fields enter the
  Cargo batch or shell_check eval. The entire directory now refuses R5 reuse.
Other .bboxy globs found by the script audit read data, not executable checks:
- scripts/pending-flags.sh:8 reads invariant status/slow/gate fields; it already
  runs in records_checks, and the directory is now also refused for reuse.
- scripts/never-block.sh:11 reads task status and blocked-on-person phrases;
  the records gate already runs it.
- scripts/quarantine.py:105 validates a task number in the administration path;
  it does not execute the task body. The quarantine table is a literal named
  input and remains covered by the existing named-record refusal.
- scripts/e2e-seed.sh:22 compares function/type/status as data in its verify
  branch, without executing text supplied by a record.
- scripts/images.sh:11 extracts image links and checks their files; the records
  gate already runs it.
- scripts/harness-submodule.py:129 restores/removes test-owned child run
  outputs; it does not execute record-supplied commands.
Other globs cover workspace/model/Rust inputs, lab/release copies, temporary
ledgers or private e2e fixture outputs. Non-.bboxy tree changes already refuse
R5. No second executable .bboxy gate-record glob was found in current scripts.
This is an audit of the present script corpus, not a promise about future gate
scripts; new dynamic executable inputs must carry equivalent refusal coverage.

Red -> green evidence
Two witnesses were added before changing production code. On the previous
6c9d9d74 implementation, with only those tests added, the corrected baseline
command exited 1 with exactly two assertion failures:
1. LandTests.test_records_gate_refuses_a_new_executable_invariant:
   "executable invariant delta was accepted". It adds a valid invariant with
   check: cargo test -p a fixture after the full gate. Old code accepted and
   pushed it. Fixed code refuses, leaves the remote unchanged, and runs zero
   Cargo checks on that path.
2. LandTests.test_records_gate_refuses_submodule_delta_despite_ignore_config:
   "ignored submodule delta was accepted". Old code returned without Refusal.
With the two production guards restored, both plus the existing unreferenced
records-only positive passed (3 tests, exit 0).
The first draft gitlink fixture used the commit helper that re-staged away its
missing gitlink; that setup error is retained in baseline-red.log. The witness
was corrected to commit its prepared index directly before the valid baseline
was captured in baseline-red-fixed-fixture.log. No production fix was present
in that valid baseline.

scripts/test-landing-budget-controls.py adds two canonical controls:
R5-executable removes only the invariant-directory refusal. The new invariant
assertion fails with exit 1; restoration gives exit 0.
R5-submodule removes only --ignore-submodules=none. The ignored-submodule
assertion fails with exit 1; restoration gives exit 0.
All 20 controls ran in the actual full make test and each went 1 -> 0 at its
named assertion. Python unittest uses exit 1 for these assertion failures.
Their source hashes were checked against a89e6f0c before archiving the logs.
These checks strengthen the existing equivalent-input predicate;
verification/contracts.toml LandingVerification and verification/README.md
record the restriction. No new state machine or parallel formal checker was
introduced. Existing R0-R4 behavior and controls remain in the same PR.

